              "id": "ocp-002",
              "severity": "SEVERE",
              "metric": "OCP-2",
              "line_start": 85,
              "line_end": 99,
              "title": "Default LogParserAdapter is untestable due to its sealed dependency on LogParser",
              "issue": "LogViewerViewModel injects LogParserAdapter as its default parser (line 88). LogParserAdapter is a struct (cannot be subclassed) and contains a sealed NON-INJECTED call to LogParser.parseMessages(at:) (a project-owned static enum). As a result, tests that receive the default wiring cannot substitute the parsing behaviour without modifying source code.",
              "impact": "LogViewerViewModel's loadMessages() cannot be tested in isolation with a controlled parser when using the default wiring. Any test must supply an alternate LogMessageParsing conformer via the designated initializer — which works — but the default path is permanently sealed to the concrete LogParser implementation.",
              "rule_source": "references/principles/OCP/rule.md — OCP-2, Testability Score"
            },
            {
              "id": "ocp-003",
              "severity": "SEVERE",
              "metric": "OCP-2",
              "line_start": 85,
              "line_end": 99,
              "title": "Default LogURLResolver is untestable due to sealed internal instantiations",
              "issue": "LogViewerViewModel injects LogURLResolver as its default URL resolver (line 91). LogURLResolver is a struct (cannot be subclassed) and internally instantiates CodexPaths, CodexRolloutStore, and calls SessionScanner.findSubagentDirs statically — none of which are injected. Tests receiving the default wiring cannot replace these collaborators.",
              "impact": "LogViewerViewModel.fileURL and the Codex-path branch of resolveURL() cannot be tested with fakes. The resolver is permanently bound to real filesystem paths and Codex storage structures unless the caller explicitly provides a substitute LogURLResolving conformer.",
              "rule_source": "references/principles/OCP/rule.md — OCP-2, Testability Score"
            }
