              "id": "ocp-004",
              "severity": "SEVERE",
              "metric": "OCP-2",
              "line_start": 217,
              "line_end": 217,
              "title": "AppSettings is an untestable final class dependency injected into LogViewerView",
              "issue": "LogViewerView accepts AppSettings as a concrete final class (line 217). AppSettings.displayMode, .maxVisibleLogMessages, .expandThinking, and .expandTools are accessed throughout the view. AppSettings is final (cannot be subclassed) and internally references UserDefaults.standard as a NON-INJECTED singleton in every property's didSet. Swapping the settings source — e.g., in tests or previews — requires either providing a live AppSettings object backed by real UserDefaults or modifying the source.",
              "impact": "LogViewerView cannot be previewed or tested with an in-memory or stub settings object. Any change to how display settings are stored (e.g., moving to a cloud-synced store) requires modifying AppSettings and all callers.",
              "rule_source": "references/principles/OCP/rule.md — OCP-2, Testability Score"
            },
